    "media:imagetext": "OZ-72-OP-098\nEFF. 8/82\n0372-7098-11\nOZARK AIRLINES\nDC-9 FAN JET\nEmergency Evacuation/Passenger Information\nNO SMOKING\nIN THE LAVATORIES\nCARRYON BAGGAGE. Federal regulations require all carryon baggage to\nbe stowed during takeoff and landing. These items must be placed under\nthe seat in front of you unless you are riding in an aircraft with enclosed\noverhead compartments. All other overhead racks may be used only for\nsuch items as coats and hats. Should you require assistance, please ask\nyour flight attendant about the stowage of these items.\nOZARK AIR LINES would like to remind its passengers that federal regula-\ntions prohibit the use of portable electronic devices on board aircraft.\nRadios and other electronic equipment may not be operated during the\nflight as they might interfere with navigation and communications equip-\nment. This does not, however, apply to the following devices: Portable\nvoice recorders, tape players,\nhearing aids, heart pacemakers, electric\nshavers, electronic watches or hand-held, solid state, electronic calculators\nor games.\nSEAT CUSHIONS. The seat cushion of each passenger seat is an ap-\nproved flotation device and may be used in the event a ditching operation\nshould become necessary.\nCIGARETTE LIGHTERS. We would like to caution our customers who\nmay have cigarette lighters with the visual fluid reservoir. Under the chang-\ning conditions of the cabin it is sometimes possible to have a very large\nflame due to a pressure buildup in this reservoir. We would advise against\nthe use of this type lighter on board the aircraft.\nSMOKERS. To ensure the comfort of all passengers, smoking is prohibited\nin certain parts of the cabin at all times. Pipe and cigar smoking are also pro-\nhibited. If you desire to smoke and are in a seat where it is not allowed,\ncheck with the flight attendant to change. Of course, smoking is prohibited\nin all areas during takeoff and landing.",
